    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0939" n="837" xml:id="pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">818.00/730</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at San José</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chase</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-06-21"><hi rendition="#italic">June 21,
                            1919</hi>.</date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July
                        2.</hi>]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 597</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that, owing to
                    the constant complaint as to Americans taking part in aid of the various
                    factions in Costa Rica, the following notice was posted in the Consulate on June
                    15, 1919.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p rendition="#center">“<hi rendition="#small-caps">notice to american
                            citizens</hi></p>
                    <p>“In the present situation of affairs in Costa Rica you are most earnestly
                        requested not to give any offence or support to any faction whether in
                        control or not.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>Copies were given to some Americans. Naturally those who are aiding Tinoco and
                    who have been doing everything they can to injure the Consul both here and at
                    home did not have copies and could only hear of it through others. No copies
                    were sent out by mail.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Benjamin F. Chase</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
